# WS-67 — Collection coded error wiring

**Target repo:** `magiq-media`
**Depends on:** MM-100 (SDK `errorCode` slot on `DomainError` + `ProblemDetails` emission)

## Problem

`docs/spec/shared/error-catalog.md § Collection` names 10 Collection error codes. Code emits every refusal as `DomainError.InvalidOperation(prose)` or `ResourceNotFound(prose)` with no `errorCode` member on the wire. Clients cannot branch on `body.errorCode` for any Collection refusal today.

The 10 codes:

| errorCode | HTTP | Condition |
|---|---|---|
| `CollectionNotFound` | 404 | Absent / wrong tenant |
| `CollectionAlreadyExists` | 409 | Name taken in tenant |
| `CollectionIdAlreadyExists` | 409 | Duplicate caller-supplied id |
| `CollectionAlreadyArchived` | 422 | Archive on archived |
| `CollectionArchived` | 422 | Any mutation on archived collection |
| `CollectionCascadeInProgress` | 409 | Archive/unarchive cascade running |
| `CascadeRunNotCurrent` | 409 | Cascade `CascadeRunId` ≠ current |
| `CascadeReportNotFound` | 422 | Un-archive with no persisted report |
| `CollectionNotArchived` | 422 | Un-archive node step on non-archived |
| `UnarchiveNameConflict` | 409 | Name live-taken since archive released it |

## Code state today

- `ArchiveCollectionHandler` returns `ResourceNotFound("Collection not found.")` and `collection.Archive()` returns `DomainError.InvalidOperation("Collection is already archived.")` — no code.
- `Collection.Rename` refuses rename on archived with `"Collection is already archived."` — maps to `CollectionArchived`.
- `CreateCollectionHandler` has no duplicate-id refusal — `CollectionIdAlreadyExists` depends on F020 (`AggregateAlreadyExistsException`, MM-032 / WS-13b).
- Collection name uniqueness: handler uses `INameReservationService.ApplyAsync` with scope `ScopeKeys.Collection`; refusal shape today is `DomainError.InvalidOperation` with reservation prose, not `CollectionAlreadyExists`.
- `CompleteCollectionArchive`, `UnarchiveCollection`, cascade-run commands do not exist in code (part of MM-031 Step-Functions saga pivot for `magiq-media-collection-archive-cascade`). Five codes (`CollectionCascadeInProgress`, `CascadeRunNotCurrent`, `CascadeReportNotFound`, `CollectionNotArchived`, `UnarchiveNameConflict`) can only be emitted once those commands land.

## What the spec requires

- A `CollectionErrorCodes` constants class carrying all 10 codes.
- Every Collection aggregate refusal returns `DomainError.<Factory>(ErrorCode = CollectionErrorCodes.<Code>, …)` (SDK slot per MM-100).
- Every `ProblemDetails` for a Collection refusal carries `errorCode` + spec `type: https://errors.magiqmedia.com/domain/<kebab>`.
- HTTP status matches the catalog row for each code.

## Implementation requirements

### Phase A — codes wired to existing commands (independent)

- Add `src/modules/Catalog/Catalog.Domain/Aggregates/Collections/CollectionErrorCodes.cs` with 10 `const string` members.
- `Collection.Archive` refusal → `CollectionAlreadyArchived`.
- `Collection.Rename`, `UpdateDescription`, `SetVisibility`, `ApplyTags`, `SetDefaultMediaProfile` refusal on archived → `CollectionArchived`.
- `ArchiveCollectionHandler`, `RenameCollectionCommandHandler`, `UpdateCollectionDescriptionHandler`, `SetCollectionVisibilityHandler`, `TagCollectionHandler`, `SetDefaultMediaProfileHandler`, `CreateCollectionCommandHandler`, `BulkCreateCollectionsHandler`: aggregate-missing → `CollectionNotFound`.
- `CreateCollectionCommandHandler` + `BulkCreateCollectionsHandler`: name reservation refusal → `CollectionAlreadyExists`.
- `CreateCollectionCommandHandler` + `BulkCreateCollectionsHandler`: duplicate caller-supplied id (via `AggregateAlreadyExistsException` once MM-032 ships) → `CollectionIdAlreadyExists`.

### Phase B — codes gated by cascade/unarchive commands (coordinate with MM-031)

- `CompleteCollectionArchive` handler + `UnarchiveCollection` handler + cascade step-handlers emit:
  - `CollectionCascadeInProgress` — concurrent run on same collection.
  - `CascadeRunNotCurrent` — cascade step's `CascadeRunId` ≠ current.
  - `CascadeReportNotFound` — un-archive requested with no persisted report.
  - `CollectionNotArchived` — un-archive node step on non-archived.
  - `UnarchiveNameConflict` — name live-taken while archived.
- These are not drafted in this plan's body — they land with the cascade/unarchive command plans. This plan carries only the `CollectionErrorCodes` constant for each; code sites raise them when the owning commands land.

## Wire-visibility

Every Collection refusal response changes shape per MM-100 — `errorCode` at root, `type` on `errors.magiqmedia.com`, HTTP status unchanged. Clients branch on `errorCode` from the day MM-107 ships; prose `title`/`detail` remain informational.

